{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"c17d7265fc5017b3","type":"group","x":-1552,"y":3040,"width":5312,"height":2080,"label":"Visit Anne"},
		{"id":"9e5d9db90ec3b1fd","type":"group","x":-5064,"y":-2353,"width":3004,"height":2193,"label":"Inbox"},
		{"id":"98b6e42d6d88bf95","type":"group","x":-1577,"y":1271,"width":3604,"height":1609,"label":"Lagistics"},
		{"id":"fa48381217b041b7","type":"group","x":-1598,"y":-120,"width":3632,"height":1138,"label":"Belonging?"},
		{"id":"07ac2475860993d0","type":"group","x":-1593,"y":-1319,"width":3173,"height":959,"label":"From Then To"},
		{"id":"dc44f63e26c2a3d4","type":"group","x":-1515,"y":5673,"width":4314,"height":2117,"label":"Camping"},
		{"id":"243f8cafecb047d6","type":"text","text":"With the popcorn, make sure Grant thinks about how it's about that Jane was helping them all along. It's not about \"oh Savanna didn't entirely reject everything\" it's about Grant knows he can trust Jane, because Jane is familiar, Jane isn't totally new. Without knowing it, a part of Jane has been there helping them all along. It's part of why Grant relaxes. He's not moving to something new, he's coming home to who he's always been. He might not have Sara's red hair, but he has her protective temperament. \n\nJane didn't know it, but she had help them get through some of the hardest times in that apartment. ","x":-4560,"y":-2080,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"9110c46b8d3581f2","type":"text","text":"Maybe Grant was the only person he knew with purple eyes, and that's part of why he notices them in Emma.\n\nAnd then he notices them in Jane. \n\nAgain building this trust, so he can let Jane worry about Ben and relax. ","x":-4120,"y":-2080,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"b7e0131626d85d90","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/Mindset.md","x":-1580,"y":-2240,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"61d9bfd67ace531a","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/09_Arriving.md","x":-780,"y":-1080,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"38fc78284ae07317","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/05_Reaping.md","x":-1400,"y":-1080,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"87b3212e0acd9b8a","type":"text","text":"I just had another little scene idea up into my head. Maybe like Grant walks in the living room and he sees Emma sitting in her ghost form curled up on like a chair or the couch or something. It's afternoon, Emma is awake. Maybe she just watching the trees out the window. Maybe Grant remembers how he was asking questions about her ghost form, and this helps him see his own curiosity. Maybe he thinks about how she talked about how it was hard to master hovering above the floor and furniture at first, and that might help give him insight about himself. She didn't understand how to do something as simple as float above a couch as though she's sitting on it at first, and yet here she is, doing so while relaxing. Maybe it helps him see that he's disoriented? She had a hard time telling which way was up, and struggled with basic things like not being in the ground. It took her time to adjust, and he needs to adjust. The rules of her existence changed, and the rules of his existence have changed. He's now struggling with things that are unfamiliar to him.","x":-260,"y":6020,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"02c3a989a4586561","type":"text","text":"Well and I'm thinking it would help give him new context, a new lense to see everything through. He doesn't know enough about psychology to reach for concepts about trauma, but he might reach certain conclusions. Like at first the nightmares don't make sense, he's in a cabin in the woods and he's safe, why is he still freaking out? Why can't he just relax and enjoy this? Why does it feel wrong? But then under the disoriented mental framework he could realize some part of him is still terrified of something bad happening to Ben, not because it might be, it isn't, but because he got so used to that. I guess it's him realizing on his own what Sara meant when she said \"he needs a break\" but realizing it in his own way. Well and realizing that this feeling isn't that something is wrong, this feeling comes from things being unfamiliar. And the more he embraces this disoriented mental framework because it's making sense, the more he is observing himself, and so the more he notices things like a mug of hot tea feels nice. And he starts to intentionally self soothe for possibly the first time in his life without having that language. Like he wouldn't call it that he wouldn't call it self soothing, but he starts doing things for himself, probably little things at first, just to help start learning and getting familiar with all the new rules of reality in life.","x":420,"y":6020,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"f3d6cf9976214ad6","type":"text","text":"I don't think he'll use the literal phasing of my body doesn't know, I think the phrasing of just some part of me is more natural. Because once he has the self-awareness to realize that there's a part of him that is still hyper worried about Ben, it doesn't fix everything overnight, but it helps him understand what's going on. It stops being confusing. Because I think on some level he would understand that it makes sense for some part of him to still be scared about Ben's safety and well-being, because well I mean he was so focused on it for so long. He comes to understand it as metaphorically sinking through the bed and the floor, because again he hasn't learned this new state yet. And maybe there is a part that gets more said out loud? He's having bad dreams sometimes, maybe Emma has at least one or two of her own during their little trip? Maybe about Savanna maybe about Brenda, maybe about both of them? Because she's still processing all of this. Maybe she basically admits that she has bad dreams about Brenda sometimes. Like he has a bad nightmare and wakes up in the middle of the night and can't get back to sleep and in the morning and I recognizes what he looks like. And he's like how did you know, and she's like I know that look. And she like makes them some tea or something. And then another morning he comes out, and he sees her, and he instantly understands what she meant by knowing that look. Because she's just been through a night of having a bad dream and not being able to go back to sleep, and he can tell. So maybe without saying anything he just starts making the tea. I have something I like with these two characters is how much they have a sort of kinship and understanding that is just unspoken. For example: Both of them have realized that they share Jane's rare eyes, neither one of them have talked about it. They don't need to. And even if she's surprised about him making her tea after her bad dream, he could just be like well that's what you made me so I assumed that helps you. If she bothers to say anything, she might not. She might not feel the need to. He does make that assumption, but she might also just figure out that he did without him needing to say anything about it.","x":1020,"y":5900,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"833987a3196ce56c","type":"text","text":"I mean maybe this will all change as I write it, but I'm sort of picturing that long-term Grant stops having the nightmares. He does adjust. It takes him a while, but he learns things other than only tea that help make him feel good, AKA communicate safety to his nervous system. Given some time that part of him learns that things are okay. And so I'm almost picturing them ending up in a role reversal of sorts, like the tea moment but on a long-term scale. And again it doesn't necessarily have to be said out loud but Grant working through all of this could almost become a model for Emma about learning to process enough to not have bad dreams about Brenda anymore. And also Grant having like these realizations and observations leads him to the natural conclusion of wanting to stay with Emma after their little camping trip. Maybe it's even Grant's idea, like he asks can I stay with you instead of Jane? And her initial response might be something like you saw my house are you sure that's what you want? And so then it becomes less about Emma being a curiosity, and more about the two of them have this shared understanding and each one can see how being around the other one benefits them. They're both doing the helpful protective because you're family thing, but on such a small scale that it's helping them not overdo it? I guess you could say accidentally learning that part that Sara was thinking about where it needs balance. They don't see it as balance, but it's the same concept underneath. And they're finding that they bring that out in each other.","x":1715,"y":6070,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"1e2a719240683087","type":"text","text":"Sara might look at them six months later and think,\n\"There it is.\"\n\"Balance.\"\nGrant and Emma would probably never use that word.","x":2393,"y":6224,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"b54d012e36dd967f","type":"text","text":"\"He's mentally losing that last sliver of the needing to hold himself together for Ben thing.\"\n\nInstead of:\n\n\"I have to hold myself together so Ben will be okay.\"\n\nIt slowly becomes:\n\n\"Ben is okay.\"","x":-820,"y":5900,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"acce361aca639f37","type":"text","text":"One nightmare that wakes him soaked in sweat, followed by Emma quietly noticing he's already awake before dawn the next morning, would say much more than seven nights in a row.\n\nThe inconsistency feels more real.\n\nSome nights he sleeps twelve hours.\n\nSome nights he barely sleeps.\n\nSome afternoons he's almost himself.\n\nOther afternoons he just... stares at the trees.\n\nRecovery isn't linear.","x":-1280,"y":5840,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"998794f3a0f968b1","type":"text","text":"I think it's going to be interesting working through all this stuff with Grant and having him occasionally visit Ben, and so then he's observing how he's reacting to being around Ben again. In small doses & visits. I'm picturing like Grant suddenly understood how Jane could so easily just smile at Ben like that, because it becomes easier for Grant. He doesn't phrase it this way but he starts reaching a point where he has the space to be authentic with Ben, the smiles start being more real and less forced. So their relationship starts to shift into a place that's healthy for Grant, as it becomes not just all about Ben. And as Ben grows and goes through the natural stages of development, I could see Ben just automatically be more curious about what's going on with you Grant? Not because he's becoming as massively curious as Grant, just because I'm not sure how to phrase it. Sure Grant was really sensitive to how Ben felt, and was really trying to respond to his feelings, but that doesn't mean Ben didn't do the same thing in a different way. Grant did more of hiding feelings Ben was more honest with his feelings, but Ben would have also been sensitive to how Grant felt. And maybe on some subconscious level or something like that, Ben wasn't asking Grant how Grant was doing because some part of been understood that wasn't on the table, Ben tried to talk about happy things in a child way of trying to cheer up Grant. Like like Ben wouldn't even be aware that he was doing it. It would be purely a subconscious kind of thing. Kind of like that same part of Ben that could tell Jane was safe automatically starts to be able to tell that Grant has the mental bandwidth to talk about himself, and again this is just something been senses automatically he doesn't even know he's doing it.","x":-1209,"y":8217,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"03b129d54918029e","type":"text","text":"Love also means letting someone carry you.","x":-2833,"y":7547,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"e4e712553a5ae2a4","type":"text","text":"I guess it is a sort of grief? It's a feeling that's hard to label for me, just this idea that he has been struggling so much for so long and there was no need for any of it. He never needed to work at all, Savanna could have come back to the family and would have been handed a house outright owned, no mortgage no rent nothing. Savanna might not have directly known that, but she never even got in contact with them, she never asked for help. She pushed them away, she attacked Emma in front of everyone. Like Jane and Sara and Anne were all there to watch. And still there was a fund for her, there was money set aside in case she ever changed her mind, well I guess from Sara's perspective more of when she changed her mind but well you know. I don't know I guess it just to me it just fits with the reaction that Sara had when she found out that Savanna was gone gone. This wasn't just a hope or a daydream, Sara assumed it was going to happen and did the necessary adult preparations, just the normal stuff that you do. This was real to Sara, she didn't know it was never going to happen.","x":1240,"y":4120,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"abc61368c49d5ed6","type":"text","text":"I feel like this \"crafty pair\" is refering to a certain memory? I mean, Emma did live in Anne's house for a time. So she's gotten to know her vampire nieces. ","x":-480,"y":3960,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"b5fe16017e93a842","type":"text","text":"Oh and meeting Anne herself is going to be a bit of a at least mental note for Grant. Because Anne is a foreign vampire she doesn't have a dark form. Yeah Grant has pieced together that Sara and Don are vampire, but they both have dark forms. He hasn't seen their fangs. They don't have fangs on a normal daily basis, they only have things in dark form not in regular form, and he's only seen them in regular form. Anne cannot hide her fangs, she has no separate form. She has fangs and glowing red eyes at all times, it's a weird quirk of her wonderfully unique biology of being turned in utero. And Emma probably won't think to warn Grant about that, because again for her it's just Tuesday. Like that's just part of her sister along with her blood red hair that she inherited from Sara. It's not abnormal and of note for Emma. And Anne is this bubbly social life it's going to be like \"Welcome darling!\" Because Anne did not get Sarah's tough nature. Anne can be ruthless, but it's completely different from her mother. Her type of ruthless is social ruthless, the kind of shark that is socialite needs to be sometimes. She knows how to play the game, but she doesn't play it when it's just family. She's completely charming and nice and friendly and proper and again giggling in her ankle length dress. Anne I will probably explain that Savanna is gone, and Anna will just be like oh my gosh I'm so sorry sweetie and hug her. It's almost a juxtaposition, she's the least normal looking one on a daily basis, but like socially probably the most normal of the bunch? At least by human standards.","x":-120,"y":3360,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"58b6ff6722e96c4e","type":"text","text":"The strongest part isn't \"wow, they're rich.\"\n\nThe strongest part is that Grant discovers what financial security actually feels like.","x":160,"y":4040,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"08153366a60d6fc8","type":"text","text":"This will really show Grant the world that he has stepped into. Because Sara and them aren't living in the woods because it's cheap. They're doing it because it fits Cass's needs, no one in his family stresses about money. ","x":-960,"y":4600,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"ba0dc42140919e15","type":"text","text":"there's like a special fund that was set aside for Savanna's return. Emma could basically mention it and be like yeah we'll probably have to pull some of Ben's half of Savanna's money, Jane will need it to buy a house for her and Ben live in. Like it could be framed from that angle of like there's a portion of the money that belongs to these two because it was set aside for Savanna, because Sara wanted to have three sources to welcome Savanna back in with open arms. I think that would really fit Sara, to have made that sort of financial decision a long time ago. Since like I said they have money to burn.","x":800,"y":4120,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"2b60f792e2b50ef3","type":"text","text":"Emma will want to stop by her own house to pack a few things, so Grant is going to get his first taste of her haunted house. Maybe even his initial reaction is that it's interesting. ","x":-1240,"y":3360,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"5030d883513b6f34","type":"text","text":"And so it's just like another complete paradigm shatter for Grant just this idea that like suddenly money is never a problem for him ever again. Like he's going to quickly understand the financial reality that yeah sure some members of the family have income, but because they choose to. We all work together we all help each other, and some of us sometimes don't have income and that's fine. Sara and Don certainly aren't working right now, and Emma's only doing the grimturn thing because she wants to not because she needs the money.","x":920,"y":3640,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"a9c750ff5756cf13","type":"text","text":"Jane is going to need a large sum of money, where does Sara want that money to come out of? That sort of thing. Sara is sort of the one in charge, but not with the like rule with an iron fist sort of way, these are her daughters. They choose to let her lead, they intentionally follow. This is genuine care, not threat of excommunicado. Anne isn't afraid she'll be punished if she doesn't get Sara's approval, Anne genuinely wants Sara's input.","x":1080,"y":4560,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"759984aa35609027","type":"text","text":"And for Grant this is probably another one of those things that should be reassuring but like on some level scares his nervous system. Every element of his concept of reality is rapidly shifting, and this is just been like what like day two day three? I think day two. Like this is a rapid shift for him, but also gives him the confidence to quit that stupid job in the city.","x":1480,"y":3640,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"c3859eecb3705bb2","type":"text","text":"I'm not seeing this as Grant being impressed with wealth or something like that, more just Grant's head is completely boggled because the concept of financial insecurity has just utterly been erased from his existence for the rest of his life. It just makes his past seems so meaningless. He has spent so much time stressing out about how to get Ben new shoes for school, when all along his extended family had a nest egg tucked away that can just casually buy a house for Ben to live in. And I mean technically it could buy a house for Grant too, but they don't make decisions the way Grant is used to making financial decisions. They make people decisions and support them with money they don't make money decisions and then try to make people work around them. Grant is used to having to fit him in Ben around the limits of money. This shows him that that entire concept just got flipped on its fucking head so hard.","x":1680,"y":4120,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"319c732da5b59490","type":"text","text":"I just sort of had this little like moment in my head of like it's just Emma and grant, and grants like um what fun were y'all talking about earlier. And Emma is like well yeah of course Sara set aside a fund for Savanna, she figured if she came back she'd probably need like a house or something, so she had money set aside. Sometimes it wasn't that much money, we had to dip into it a bit when everyone split up, I guess that could have been when you were like a baby, but Sara made sure to refill it afterwards. That's where she put almost all of the money from those fat paychecks she got while she was in the military. The rocket was built mostly with my paychecks as a scientist. ","x":2120,"y":4120,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"c008545dd8b460ba","type":"text","text":"Well yes of course they're not going to be all hushed tones about him or around him about the money. He's one of them. There is no question about rather he's part of the family. He's a teenager he's old enough to hear these things.","x":3200,"y":3640,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"97ddc783d9a05922","type":"text","text":"Because like I'm picturing how Grant would feel about that, just this idea that Sara was throwing her paychecks into a fund that is now for him when she didn't even know he existed. Like he would recognize that that's someone working to take care of him, similar to that the popcorn recipe with Jane we're just like oh well Jane was always there, Sara was always there it was just completely invisible because it was a savings fund that he knew nothing about.\n\nBecause knowing a lot of it came from when Sara was in the military might make him feel like it's Sara's money, but Sara insisted the Savanna Fund be split in half and that one of those halves is Grant's. Like I said maybe they have to dip into Grant's half a little bit to get a house for Ben, but Grant won't care about that. Especially in the state he's in right now, he'd probably give the whole thing if Ben needed it. \n\nI'm also thinking that at first this might scare grant. He's used to the other two drops, he's used to favors come with strings. He thinks he doesn't understand Sarah and it scares him. But the thing is he actually understands her better than he knows. Because he's been doing the same exact thing for Ben, being there just because he's family. He didn't actually have to take care of the kid. He didn't technically have to be the adult in the situation. But in Grant's mind there was no other choice on the table. Which is very similar to how Sara sees thing in such situations. \"Because you're on my crew, why are we still talking about this?\" type of mindset. The \"well duh, you're family.\" ","x":2560,"y":4120,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"a77379acc5650054","type":"text","text":"Emma could be like well we need to go pick up the camping gear from my young sister's house, her house is bigger so we store things there. And Grant is completely caught off guard by Emma's casual \"bigger\" when he sees it. \n\nMaybe Emma would give him some sort of warning of like \"Oh by the way and lives with her two daughters and her now wife, but maybe don't go into a room alone with their two daughters?\"\n\n\"Why? Is there something wrong with her daughters?\"\n\n\"No, they got their fangs as toddlers.\"\n\n\"And how old are her daughters now?\"\n\n\"They're your age, but they're still children.\"\n\n\"I'm not a kid.\" And he wasn't about to be treated like one. \n\n\"No, but they are. They're nice kids, but they're also a crafty pair.\" Emma chuckled. ","x":-680,"y":3360,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"fd0a95831cd42344","type":"text","text":"Because Emma's younger sister and lives in a Ravenwood Manor, the big one in the southern part of the map that like by default isn't inhabited. In my story she fixed it up and turned it into the proper elite mansion befitting a socialite. ","x":-880,"y":3960,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"d53dab695d9d3097","type":"text","text":"Grant initially looks for Ben, and Jane has tucked Ben in for a nap because his little system needs a break. \n\nMaybe they get outside.\n\nIdk, I might prefer the \"where's Ben?\" \"Oh I already laid him down to sleep in my tent over there\" type of sequence.","x":-1240,"y":2140,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"ca9abb38154318e7","type":"text","text":"they're in the Ravenwood Manor, Anne Emma Grant Kaylee they're together in you know some sort of room sitting on couches something like that. And kind of like a side note Emma mentioned oh yeah Jane will be by later today she needs to buy a house so she'll need money, and Anne's like do you know how much so I can get the paperwork ready, and Emma's like well I'm really not sure she's out looking for a place right now, she wants to see what Ben wants to do see what's best for the kid, maybe a hundred thousand or two I don't think she's going to go for that big of a place. And like at least internally Grant's jaw drops through the floor. This woman is casually talking about $100,000. Probably one of those things were in the moment Grant is simply observing, but I think that's a thing that like he's not going to be able to be quiet about when it's just him and Emma alone again. And maybe Emma is basically like well yeah whenever you look to buy a house just come talk to and she'll make the numbers work and we'll get you something, probably when you're older though. I mean I guess if you really want your own house as a teenager we can talk about it, but like I'm not sure living alone is the best thing for you right now. And Grant might basically be like I can just walk in there and ask her for that kind of money, and Emma's like well yeah you're part of the family duh. You're a Yootz hun.","x":920,"y":3160,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"50faa898f27b48e9","type":"text","text":"fat checks when they were in the military","x":2240,"y":3360,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"9aa332daabffa4ff","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/24_Laptop.md","x":1520,"y":1600,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"ffe77a2f043871cc","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/22.1_MorningTea.md","x":-260,"y":1600,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"c0b787dc76e22607","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/21_GoGhost.md","x":-680,"y":1600,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"f0bb441e97b415a5","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/20_BenAsleep.md","x":-1240,"y":1600,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"69ed22a06ea31e34","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/23_SleepingIn.md","x":620,"y":1600,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"90bb1aa5807f25fd","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/22.2_MorningPancakes.md","x":160,"y":1600,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"15ffb32f23952a57","type":"text","text":"Okay so I just realized I have Jane and Ben there and then suddenly Jane and Ben have been gone for a while. Time space continuum whoopsie. Maybe it's just that Jane was in the cabin, and so Ben wandered off to the cabin to go tell her that Grant's awake and wanting food, and maybe she's already making like lunch or something? I don't know or maybe she was around the fire with Emma and ben, again not fire lit it's the middle of the day, but Ben heard Grant stirring, Ben came into the tent, grant talked about food, been totaled back out of the tent until Jane that Grant wanted food and so they've headed off to the cabin to cook something, and that's why like it's just Emma that's there when Grant comes out of the tent or like is finished using the bathroom or whatever, and Grant might ask where Ben is at, or just confirm that he's in the cabin or something. Or maybe he's too stressed out about the school in the laptops to think about that? Like it's actually his defenses coming down one by one, but they are coming but it's one by one so like the constantly track Ben's location has come down, but the make sure the school is informed has not. And Emma could say that like you know Jane was planning on taking Ben with her to look at places later today, and then in her head she's thinking because we didn't want you to wake up and him not be here because we figured you wouldn't like that. And most of the conversation still goes the same about talking about going camping in granite falls instead of gibbi point. ","x":1080,"y":1600,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"c745b2a2dd71f5e7","type":"text","text":"The hand-rubbing payoff for later:\n\nBecause that's how Grant operates: He notices things without immediately commenting on them.\n\n----\n\nThen, later, Emma starts rubbing her hands again.\n\nGrant just says something like, \"You can phase if you need to.\"\n\nEmma looks over. \"What?\"\n\n\"You always rub your hands first.\"\n\n----\n\nThat's a fantastic payoff. It rewards attentive readers exactly the same way it rewards Emma. It also tells Emma something she probably hasn't realized: Someone has been paying attention to her.","x":2280,"y":1040,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"c945bef325d58f5b","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/11_Cooking.md","x":-1380,"y":0,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"47107e9c53ce3ac7","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/12_FamilyTree.md","x":-840,"y":0,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"e2b3c863f69d5317","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/13_RestMyEyes.md","x":-280,"y":0,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"a2c2d4bddea91ac7","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/16_CabinMeal.md","x":1280,"y":0,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"71f397331cd65956","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/15_Sara.md","x":800,"y":0,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"928e44cc5dee642b","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/14_JaneWasAlwaysHelping.md","x":320,"y":0,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"fc057a28091f7704","x":-840,"y":560,"width":400,"height":400,"type":"text","text":"Actually maybe the landlord would take in Grant, but only Grant. And maybe use Mckinley, because really Grant doesn't remember her much, so she's not \"mom\"\n\nGrant probably doesn't think of Savanna as a competent mother, but probably calls her mom especially around Ben just to make things simple. Savanna was the one \"raising\" him even before Mckinley died anyway. Savanna tried to give her daughter the chance to be a teenager, and then her daughter died. "}
	],
